Z||000006||gixxer||11-07-2000||07:05 PM||||First off, Civic engines turn backwards from everything else, so there might be some problems there. <BR>Secondly, if the blower is sized for a 1.6L engine, it may have to be oversped considerably to feed a 2.5L or 2.8L engine. If you spin the blower too fast, it will become very inefficient and put out loads of heat. <BR>I think this is a poor idea, and you should just talk to the people at Vortech and see what they can come up with. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||11-08-2000||09:02 AM||||Magnusen M62, M90, Vortech A/B/S/T trim ATI P600b they will all support our 2.8s some better than others. (get a hold of BBBAD GT for flow charactoristics of the superchargers... he has it in an Excel format)||||reg||1
